MOST of the games in this directory are Berkeley's, and none of them is this
project's or covered by the repository's root LICENSE.  This file exists
because the tree had no directory-level statement of that; the authority is, as
always, the notice each source file carries.  Nothing here was granted by
anyone working on this port.

This file used to open "The games in this directory are Berkeley's".  That was
wrong for four of them, and a blanket claim that is wrong is worse than none:
see "Not Berkeley's at all" below before relying on the terms in this file for
any particular game.

Provenance
----------

The base is bsd-games 2.17 (Joseph S. Myers, 2005-02-18), the Debian/NetBSD
collection -- 142 of the 155 .c/.h still carry a `$NetBSD: ... $' revision tag,
and most also carry an `@(#)... (Berkeley)' SCCS line.  They have been edited
for this port (K&R declarations, 16-bit int, the COHERENT curses), which
changes nothing about whose code it is.  bsd-games itself is a collection: it
holds no copyright over the games it collects, and the packaging files it adds
are its own (see quiz.db/Makefrag, quoted in ../lib/COPYING).

