Copyright years vary by file, from 1980 to 1994.

Exceptions found in this directory
----------------------------------

  adventure/	`extern.h' carries the older FOUR-clause form, whose third
		condition is the advertising requirement:

		    3. All advertising materials mentioning features or use
		       of this software must display the following
		       acknowledgement: This product includes software
		       developed by the University of California, Berkeley
		       and its contributors.

		It also carries `Copyright (c) 1997 Christos Zoulas.  All
		rights reserved.'  Read that file before assuming the
		three-clause text above applies to adventure.

  atc/		additionally `Copyright (c) 1987 by Ed James', with its own
		conditions in the file headers.

  scripts/	`wargames' is a rewrite of bsd-games' wargames.sh for a shell
		with no `echo -n' and no comment lexer, and the port dropped
		its notice.  Restored 2026-08-04, verbatim from bsd-games
		2.17, carried as `:' lines because a `#' line is EXECUTED by
		this system's sh.  It is the FOUR-clause form, with the
		advertising acknowledgement.

  canfield/	NetBSD's revision of Berkeley's canfield, so the terms above
		apply.  `../cfscores.c', its betting-record reader, comes from
		the 4.3BSD 5.8 copy in the COHERENT-mirror holding instead and
		carries the older, shorter Regents grant of 1983 in its own
		header; canfield.c says why the two came from different
		places.

Not Berkeley's at all
---------------------

Three of the programs built out of this directory did not come from BSD, and
the terms above do not reach them.

  tetris/	Copyright 1989 Phill Everson & Martyn Shortley and Copyright
		1989 Roberto Biancardi; comp.sources.games v8, COHERENT port
		by Matt Kimmel and later Udo Munk.  Upstream's terms are
		vendored verbatim at tetris/COPYRIGHT and each source now
		names them.  They are NOT BSD and NOT Free: the notice and any
		statement of authorship must be reproduced on all copies, no
		fee may be charged without the authors' written permission,
		and the software may not be sold, rented, leased or traded.
		A distributor must pass the same permission on.  This project
		distributes an image at no charge, which is what the notice
		permits; anyone doing otherwise must read tetris/COPYRIGHT
		first.

  gomoku/	ORIGIN AND TERMS UNKNOWN.  Neither our copy nor the holding it
		came from (the MWC BBS collection) carries a copyright notice,
		an author, or a grant of any kind, and no notice is invented
		here to fill the gap.  It is not Berkeley's -- NetBSD's gomoku
		is a different program and was not used -- and it is not this
		project's.  An open item, recorded rather than settled.

  cfscores.c	see the canfield/ entry above.

  fortune.c	Mark Williams Company's own fortune(1), taken unaltered from
		the post-4.2 COHERENT source.  It is the one file in this
		directory that IS covered by the repository's root LICENSE,
		and its database (../lib/fortunes) is MWC's too.

Other directories in this tree with the same lineage but no COPYING of their
own: ../net/hunt (Regents, 1983-2003, three-clause) and the individual BSD
commands scattered under ../../cmd -- finger, host, rlogin, snake, worm.
../../cmd/rlogin and ../../net/resolv carry the four-clause form.

